<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float">Listing 3: </span>Example of expanded program after linking.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Each <span id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">UI_CALL</span> placeholder (e.g., <span id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">[28]: Read all Comments</span>) is expanded into its corresponding low-level actions (e.g., <span id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">read_text_all selector="article.comment"</span>).
Symbolic variables like <span id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">@manager_name</span> and <span id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">@reply_text</span> remain as placeholders, carrying <span id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">input</span> annotations that will be resolved in the compilation stage.
The control flow structure (<span id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">if-else</span>) is preserved exactly as specified in the sketch IR.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.3. </span>Compiling into Executable Plans</h3>

<div id="S4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Once all resolvable <span id="S4.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">UI_CALL</span>s have been linked, the system compiles the resulting program into an executable representation that is type-safe, execution-ready, and supports runtime symbolic binding.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The compiler first performs instruction expansion.
Each linked SMG operation is expanded into a fixed sequence of primitive browser actions implemented via Playwright (e.g., <span id="S4.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Sort by New</span> <math id="S4.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> {<span id="S4.SS3.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">click(#sort)</span>, <span id="S4.SS3.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">click(#new)</span>}).
This produces a fully specified Python program with no abstract UI calls.
The compiler also extracts helper functions via AST analysis and hoists them to a root-level Python Node, ensuring helper logic is initialized before the main execution flow begins.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The expanded program is converted into a <span id="S4.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">MixedActionPlan</span> object graph.
The plan consists of three node types:</p>
<ul id="S4.SS3.p3.2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><math id="S4.I1.i1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bullet" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∙</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bullet</annotation></semantics></math></span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">UI Nodes:</span> Store primitive browser actions (e.g., click, fill) with associated locators or selectors. Besides storing a <em id="S4.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">single</em> primitive action, an UI node may also contain symbolic bindings (e.g., <span id="S4.I1.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">@worcester_forum_name</span>) that are resolved at runtime. Based on that, <span id="S4.I1.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">ActionEngine</span> will run UI Nodes one by one, which will easily trigger validator(see section <a href="#S5.SS1" title="5.1. Execution and Validation ‣ 5. Runtime Execution and Adaptation ‣ ActionEngine: From Reactive to Programmatic GUI Agents via State Machine Memory" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a>) when a specific UI Node failed.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><math id="S4.I1.i2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bullet" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∙</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bullet</annotation></semantics></math></span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Python Nodes:</span> Encapsulate local computation and produce explicitly named output variables for data flow tracking.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><math id="S4.I1.i3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bullet" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∙</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bullet</annotation></semantics></math></span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Control Flow Nodes:</span> Map <span id="S4.I1.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">for</span>/<span id="S4.I1.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">if</span>/<span id="S4.I1.i3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">while</span> to container nodes preserving nesting structure in the IR.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Each node carries its execution context, code logic, and data binding requirements.</p>
</div>
<section id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Running Example (Final Executable Plan)</h5>

<div id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">After compilation, the program is transformed into a <span id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">MixedActionPlan</span> with typed nodes. <a href="#listing4" title="Listing 4 ‣ Running Example (Final Executable Plan) ‣ 4.3. Compiling into Executable Plans ‣ 4. Execution Agent ‣ ActionEngine: From Reactive to Programmatic GUI Agents via State Machine Memory" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> shows an excerpt of the structure (simplified from the full 25-node plan).
The plan demonstrates the three node types: (1) Python Nodes containing helper functions and orchestration logic; (2) UI Nodes with actions (<span id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">read_text_all</span>, <span id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">fill</span>, <span id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">click</span>) mapped to Playwright locators/selectors, with symbolic inputs such as <span id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">["@reply_message"]</span>; (3) Conditional Nodes enabling branching logic with nested action sequences.
At runtime, when the Executor encounters <span id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">"input": ["@target_index"]</span>, it resolves the symbol against the local context—where <span id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">target_index</span> was set by the preceding Python Node—and generates the concrete Playwright command with the bound value.</p>
</div>
